From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:29:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: Refuse S5L8960X DMA windows that aren't
 base-aligned
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An S5L8960X DART sees IOVAs relative to the base of its DMA window.
Behind the A9 PCIe root complex (window 0x80000000 + 0x3c000000), the
NVMe admin submission queue at IOVA 0xbbffe000 faulted at DART address
0x3bffe000. apple-dart indexes its tables the same way by masking the
window base off the IOVA (mask = ~dma_min), which equals subtracting it
only if the base is aligned beyond the size of the window.

Refuse a window that doesn't satisfy this when the domain is finalized,
instead of silently translating through the wrong table entries. The
windows in use (0x80000000 + 0x3c000000 and + 0x3ffff000) pass.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 320a9f63 (J71t ledger 1.4); only the
 alignment check, the window comes from the five-cell DMA window
 specifier (ledger 1.5), checked before the page tables are allocated]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 2e23a3722..6d764cc29 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -879,6 +879,21 @@ static int apple_dart_finalize_domain(struct apple_dart_domain *dart_domain,
 	if (dart_domain->finalized)
 		goto done;
 
+	/*
+	 * S5L8960X DARTs see IOVAs relative to the window base: behind the A9
+	 * PCIe root complex, IOVA 0xbbffe000 of the window at 0x80000000
+	 * reaches the DART as 0x3bffe000. The tables are indexed the same way
+	 * by masking the base off below, which equals subtracting it only if
+	 * the base is aligned beyond the window size.
+	 */
+	if (dart->hw->type == DART_S5L8960X && cfg->dma_min &&
+	    cfg->dma_max - cfg->dma_min >= (cfg->dma_min & -cfg->dma_min)) {
+		dev_err(dart->dev, "DMA window %pad..%pad is not base-aligned\n",
+			&cfg->dma_min, &cfg->dma_max);
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto done;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < MAX_DARTS_PER_DEVICE; ++i) {
 		dart_domain->stream_maps[i].dart = cfg->stream_maps[i].dart;
 		for (j = 0; j < BITS_TO_LONGS(dart->num_streams); j++)
